{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgumwxe4kxWdYwPdEgcqS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Keeper of Saltmere Light\n\nFor forty-one years, Elspeth Varrow climbed the 163 iron steps of Saltmere Light each evening, lit the great lamp, and turned its lens so the beam could sweep across the black water. Ships passed in the dark because of her. She rarely thought of it as heroism. It was simply the work.\n\nWhen the mainland council announced that the light would be automated, Elspeth received the letter with a steady hand. She read it twice, folded it, and went up the stairs as usual that evening.\n\nThe new system arrived in spring: a squat gray box, humming and blinking, with a satellite dish bolted to the gallery rail. Engineers showed her the screens. She nodded politely and asked where they planned to put the k"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":137,"cache_read_input_tokens":21903,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":137},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92710734-686c-4250-936c-3c306f444089","uuid":"18aa4bb1-61f1-4445-859a-d81c8fd9ce1a","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:10:14.785Z","request_id":"req_011CgumwxRRPXMHvGpXqyk2v","aborted":true}
